Z||000001||SLAMMED87GT||12-29-2001||11:07 AM||||I wouldn't say they are the answer to the Fiero as the Reatta is also a GM product. Just a luxury 2 seater car that GM wanted to market!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> That is what they were-I've been in one and it was quite comfortable, not to mention the electronic "control center" it has on the dash. Put some decent rims on one and it would be sweet. Would be tuff to get any aftermarket stuff I would think though......<P>BTW, I remember these having a 3800 in them from the factory correct. I see a Northstar conversion!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||14
